From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:17:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/31] fix(midea): map J15 robot error codes from firmware
 table

Correct the message, subsystem and severity of 1-19, 1-20, 1-21, 1-22,
1-23, 1-24, 1-81 and 1-83 to what manager_node's error tables say
(docking failed, vibrating mop fault, LDS UART failure, main board <->
motor controller UART failure, motor controller internal error,
relocalization failed, bumper keeps triggering, cliff sensor stop).

Add the codes that were reported as "Unknown error": 1-25..1-30, 1-86,
1-95, 1-165 and 1-168..1-172.

Based on static analysis of the firmware error tables; untested on the
robot. The wording of the turnplate and obstacle-crossing wheel entries
is derived from the internal names only. 1-43 is left alone.

